r-side for ${presetId}.`);\n121:     }\n122:     const input = parseRequestGeneration(sanitized);\n123:     const registered = await assertRegisteredPartyDevice(this.db, input);\n124:     if (registered.channel.status !== \"active\") throw new BackendError(\"FORBIDDEN\", \"Channel is not active for this party.\");\n125:     // Consent-bound request gate: the guest photo must be eligible right now.\n126:     // The worker and the publication transaction recheck before submitting and\n127:     // before publishing, so a withdrawal races fail closed.\n128:     let guest: GuestMediaDoc | undefined;\n129:     if (input.guestMediaId) {\n130:       guest = await assertGuestEligible(this.db, input, input.guestMediaId, this.now().getTime());\n131:     }\n132:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, input.partyId, input.jobId);\n133:     const result = await this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n134:       const existing = await transaction.get(ref);\n135:       if (existing.exists) {\n136:         const old = existing.data()!;\n137:         if (old.idempotencyKey !== input.idempotencyKey || old.deviceId !== input.deviceId || old.channelId !== input.channelId ||\n138:             (old.guestMediaId ?? undefined) !== (input.guestMediaId ?? undefined) ||\n139:             (old.rehearsalOnly === true) !== rehearsalOnly) {\n140:           throw new BackendError(\"FORBIDDEN\", \"jobId is already bound to a different request.\");\n141:         }\n142:         return {\n143:           state: String(old.state),\n144:           created: false,\n145:           manifestVersion: Number(old.manifestVersion),\n146:           timestamp: old.timestamp,\n147:         };\n148:       }\n149:       const inFlight = await transaction.get(\n150:         this.db.collection(`parties/${input.partyId}/jobs`).where(\"state\", \"in\", [\"queued\", \"running\"]).limit(1),\n151:       );\n152:       if (!inFlight.empty) throw new BackendError(\"BUDGET_EXCEEDED\", \"One generation is already in flight for this party.\");\n153:       await transaction.get(budgetRef(this.db, input.partyId));\n154:       const current = await transaction.get(currentManifestRef(this.db, input.partyId, input.channelId));\n155:       const sourceManifestVersion = current.exists ? Number(current.data()?.version ?? 0) : 0;\n156:       if (!Number.isSafeInteger(sourceManifestVersion) || sourceManifestVersion < 0 || (current.exists && sourceManifestVersion < 1)) {\n157:         throw new BackendError(\"MANIFEST_MISMATCH\", \"Current manifest version is invalid.\");\n158:       }\n159:       const manifestVersion = sourceManifestVersion + 1;\n160:       if (!Number.isSafeInteger(manifestVersion)) throw new BackendError(\"MANIFEST_MISMATCH\", \"Next manifest version is invalid.\");\n161:       const timestamp = FieldValue.serverTimestamp();\n162:       const cameraAttempts = Object.fromEntries(REQUIRED_CAMERA_IDS.map((cameraId) => [cameraId, {\n163:         consumedAttempt: false,\n164:         submissionState: \"not_started\",\n165:       }]));\n166:       // Re-verify consent inside the creation transaction so a withdrawal that\n167:       // lands between the pre-check and the job write fails the request.\n168:       let guestBinding: Record<string, unknown> | undefined;\n169:       if (input.guestMediaId && guest) {\n170:         const guestSnap = await transaction.get(\n171:           this.db.doc(`parties/${input.partyId}/guestMedia/${input.guestMediaId}`),\n172:         );\n173:         const current = guestSnap.exists ? (guestSnap.data() as GuestMediaDoc) : undefined;\n174:         if (!current || current.status !== \"eligible\" ||\n175:             current.sourceHash !== guest.sourceHash ||\n176:             current.consentRevision !== guest.consentRevision ||\n177:             current.deviceId !== input.deviceId || current.channelId !== input.channelId) {\n178:           throw new BackendError(\"FORBIDDEN\", \"Guest consent is no longer eligible for generation.\");\n179:         }\n180:         guestBinding = {\n181:           submissionId: input.guestMediaId,\n182:           objectPath: guest.objectPath,\n183:           sourceHash: guest.sourceHash,\n184:           sourceGeneration: guest.sourceGeneration ?? null,\n185:           consentRevision: guest.consentRevision,\n186:           deviceId: guest.deviceId,\n187:           channelId: guest.channelId,\n188:         };\n189:         // Fail closed if a fetchable URL ever reaches the persistence path.\n190:         assertNoSignedReferenceUrl(guestBinding);\n191:       }\n192:       transaction.create(ref, {\n193:         jobId: input.jobId,\n194:         partyId: registered.partyId,\n195:         deviceId: registered.deviceId,\n196:         channelId: registered.channelId,\n197:         manifestVersion,\n198:         sourceManifestVersion,\n199:         state: \"queued\",\n200:         status: \"queued\",\n201:         timestamp,\n202:         createdAt: timestamp,\n203:         idempotencyKey: input.idempotencyKey,\n204:         presetId: input.presetId,\n205:         modelId: input.presetId === CAMEO_DEMO_PRESET.presetId ? CAMEO_DEMO_PRESET.modelId : CHEAP_DEMO_PRESET.modelId,\n206:         ...(rehearsalOnly ? { rehearsalOnly: true as const } : {}),\n207:         ...(guestBinding ? { guestMedia: guestBinding, guestMediaId: input.guestMediaId } : {}),\n208:         costEstimate: input.presetId === CAMEO_DEMO_PRESET.presetId\n209:           ? { modelId: CAMEO_DEMO_PRESET.modelId, presetId: CAMEO_DEMO_PRESET.presetId, secondsOut: CAMEO_DEMO_PRESET.secondsOut }\n210:           : { modelId: CHEAP_DEMO_PRESET.modelId, presetId: CHEAP_DEMO_PRESET.presetId, secondsOut: CHEAP_DEMO_PRESET.secondsOut },\n211:         expiresAt: Timestamp.fromDate(new Date(this.now().getTime() + MEDIA_RETENTION_MS)),\n212:         cameraAttempts,\n213:         providerTasks: {},\n214:         stagedOutputs: {},\n215:       });\n216:       transaction.set(budgetRef(this.db, input.partyId), {\n217:         activeJobId: input.jobId,\n218:         state: \"in_flight\",\n219:         updatedAt: timestamp,\n220:       }, { merge: true });\n221:       for (const cameraId of REQUIRED_CAMERA_IDS) {\n222:         transaction.create(this.db.doc(usageLedgerPath({\n223:           partyId: input.partyId,\n224:           deviceId: input.deviceId,\n225:           channelId: input.channelId,\n226:           manifestVersion,\n227:           idempotencyKey: input.idempotencyKey,\n228:           jobId: input.jobId,\n229:           cameraId,\n230:         })), usageIntentDocument({\n231:           partyId: input.partyId,\n232:           deviceId: input.deviceId,\n233:           channelId: input.channelId,\n234:           manifestVersion,\n235:           idempotencyKey: input.idempotencyKey,\n236:           jobId: input.jobId,\n237:           cameraId,\n238:         }, timestamp, input.presetId === CAMEO_DEMO_PRESET.presetId ? CAMEO_DEMO_PRESET : CHEAP_DEMO_PRESET));\n239:       }\n240:       return { state: \"queued\", created: true, manifestVersion, timestamp };\n241:     });\n242:     const persisted = (await ref.get()).data();\n243:     return {\n244:       jobId: input.jobId,\n245:       partyId: input.partyId,\n246:       deviceId: input.deviceId,\n247:       channelId: input.channelId,\n248:       state: result.state,\n249:       created: result.created,\n250:       manifestVersion: result.manifestVersion,\n251:       timestamp: exposedTimestamp(persisted?.timestamp ?? result.timestamp),\n252:       idempotencyKey: input.idempotencyKey,\n253:     };\n254:   }\n255: \n256:   async getJob(partyId: string, jobId: string): Promise<FirebaseFirestore.DocumentData> {\n257:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, validateId(partyId, \"partyId\"), validateId(jobId, \"jobId\"));\n258:     const snapshot = await ref.get();\n259:     if (!snapshot.exists) throw new BackendError(\"NOT_FOUND\", \"Generation job does not exist.\");\n260:     return snapshot.data()!;\n261:   }\n262: \n263:   async getGenerationStatus(value: unknown): Promise<Record<string, unknown>> {\n264:     if (!value || typeof value !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(value)) throw new BackendError(\"INVALID_ARGUMENT\", \"Status query must be an object.\");\n265:     extractRehearsalOnly(value);\n266:     const query = stripRehearsalOnly(value) as Record<string, unknown>;\n267:     validatePresetControls(query);\n268:     if (\"prompt\" in query) {\n269:       const presetId = query.presetId === CAMEO_DEMO_PRESET.presetId ? \"cameo_demo\" : \"cheap_demo\";\n270:       throw new BackendError(\"INVALID_ARGUMENT\", `Generation prompts are fixed server-side for ${presetId}.`);\n271:     }\n272:     const input: RequestGenerationInput = parseRequestGeneration({ ...query, presetId: query.presetId ?? \"cheap_demo\" });\n273:     const registered = await assertRegisteredPartyDevice(this.db, input);\n274:     if (registered.channel.status !== \"active\") throw new BackendError(\"FORBIDDEN\", \"Channel is not active for this party.\");\n275:     const job = await this.getJob(input.partyId, input.jobId);\n276:     if (job.idempotencyKey !== input.idempotencyKey || job.deviceId !== input.deviceId || job.channelId !== input.channelId) {\n277:       throw new BackendError(\"FORBIDDEN\", \"Job status identity does not match the request.\");\n278:     }\n279:     return {\n280:       jobId: input.jobId,\n281:       partyId: job.partyId,\n282:       deviceId: job.deviceId,\n283:       channelId: job.channelId,\n284:       manifestVersion: job.manifestVersion,\n285:       timestamp: exposedTimestamp(job.timestamp),\n286:       idempotencyKey: job.idempotencyKey,\n287:       state: job.state,\n288:       status: job.status ?? job.state,\n289:       errorCode: job.errorCode,\n290:       reconciliationReason: job.reconciliationReason,\n291:     };\n292:   }\n293: \n294:   /** Records a task queue failure without allowing the worker to auto-retry it. */\n295:   async failEnqueue(task: GenerationTask): Promise<void> {\n296:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, task.partyId, task.jobId);\n297:     const budget = budgetRef(this.db, task.partyId);\n298:     await this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n299:       const [snapshot, budgetSnapshot] = await Promise.all([transaction.get(ref), transaction.get(budget)]);\n300:       if (!snapshot.exists) throw new BackendError(\"NOT_FOUND\", \"Generation job does not exist.\");\n301:       const job = snapshot.data()!;\n302:       if (job.idempotencyKey !== task.idempotencyKey || job.deviceId !== task.deviceId || job.channelId !== task.channelId) {\n303:         throw new BackendError(\"FORBIDDEN\", \"Task identity does not match the job.\");\n304:       }\n305:       const timestamp = FieldValue.serverTimestamp();\n306:       if (job.state === \"queued\") {\n307:         transaction.update(ref, {\n308:           state: \"failed\",\n309:           status: \"failed\",\n310:           errorCode: \"PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE\",\n311:           enqueueFailedAt: timestamp,\n312:           failedAt: timestamp,\n313:           timestamp,\n314:         });\n315:         if (budgetSnapshot.exists && budgetSnapshot.data()?.activeJobId === task.jobId) {\n316:           transaction.update(budget, { activeJobId: null, state: \"idle\", updatedAt: timestamp });\n317:         }\n318:       } else {\n319:         // A queue response can be lost after acceptance. Preserve a worker that\n320:         // already claimed the job, while keeping the ambiguous enqueue visible.\n321:         transaction.update(ref, { enqueueErrorCode: \"PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE\", enqueueFailedAt: timestamp, timestamp });\n322:       }\n323:     });\n324:   }\n325: \n326:   async claimWorker(task: GenerationTask, leaseMs = 20 * 60 * 1000): Promise<{ claimed: boolean; job: FirebaseFirestore.DocumentData }> {\n327:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, task.partyId, task.jobId);\n328:     return this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n329:       const snapshot = await transaction.get(ref);\n330:       if (!snapshot.exists) throw new BackendError(\"NOT_FOUND\", \"Generation job does not exist.\");\n331:       const job = snapshot.data()!;\n332:       if (job.idempotencyKey !== task.idempotencyKey || job.deviceId !== task.deviceId || job.channelId !== task.channelId) {\n333:         throw new BackendError(\"FORBIDDEN\", \"Worker identity does not match the job.\");\n334:       }\n335:       if ([\"ready\", \"delivering\", \"failed\", \"expired\", \"purged\"].includes(String(job.state))) return { claimed: false, job }; // delivering is terminal for the worker: the ACK path owns the job from here.\n336:       const leaseUntil = Number(job.workerLeaseUntilMs ?? 0);\n337:       if (job.state === \"running\" && leaseUntil > this.now().getTime()) return { claimed: false, job };\n338:       const next = this.now().getTime() + leaseMs;\n339:       transaction.update(ref, {\n340:         state: \"running\",\n341:         status: \"running\",\n342:         workerLeaseUntilMs: next,\n343:         startedAt: job.startedAt ?? FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n344:         timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n345:       });\n346:       return { claimed: true, job: { ...job, state: \"running\", workerLeaseUntilMs: next } };\n347:     });\n348:   }\n349: \n350:   async heartbeat(partyId: string, jobId: string, leaseMs = 20 * 60 * 1000): Promise<void> {\n351:     await jobRef(this.db, partyId, jobId).update({ workerLeaseUntilMs: this.now().getTime() + leaseMs, timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp() });\n352:   }\n353: \n354:   async beginSubmission(partyId: string, jobId: string, cameraId: CameraId): Promise<boolean> {\n355:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, partyId, jobId);\n356:     return this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n357:       const snapshot = await transaction.get(ref);\n358:       if (!snapshot.exists) throw new BackendError(\"NOT_FOUND\", \"Generation job does not exist.\");\n359:       const job = snapshot.data()!;\n360:       const task = (job.providerTasks ?? {})[cameraId] as Record<string, unknown> | undefined;\n361:       if (typeof task?.taskId === \"string\") return false;\n362:       const attempts = { ...(job.cameraAttempts ?? {}) } as Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>;\n363:       const attempt = attempts[cameraId] ?? {};\n364:       if (attempt.consumedAttempt === true) {\n365:         if (attempt.submissionState === \"submitting\") {\n366:           throw new BackendError(\"PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE\", \"Provider submission outcome is unknown; automatic resubmission is disabled.\");\n367:         }\n368:         throw new BackendError(\"PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE\", \"Provider submission attempt has already been consumed.\");\n369:       }\n370:       attempts[cameraId] = {\n371:         ...attempt,\n372:         consumedAttempt: true,\n373:         submissionState: \"submitting\",\n374:         submissionStartedAt: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n375:       };\n376:       transaction.update(ref, { cameraAttempts: attempts, timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp() });\n377:       return true;\n378:     });\n379:   }\n380: \n381:   async recordSubmission(\n382:     partyId: string,\n383:     jobId: string,\n384:     cameraId: CameraId,\n385:     taskId: string,\n386:   ): Promise<void> {\n387:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, partyId, jobId);\n388:     await this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n389:       const snapshot = await transaction.get(ref);\n390:       if (!snapshot.exists) throw new BackendError(\"NOT_FOUND\", \"Generation job does not exist.\");\n391:       const job = snapshot.data()!;\n392:       const old = (job.providerTasks ?? {})[cameraId] as Record<string, unknown> | undefined;\n393:       if (typeof old?.taskId === \"string\" && old.taskId !== taskId) {\n394:         throw new BackendError(\"FORBIDDEN\", \"A different provider task is already persisted for this camera.\");\n395:       }\n396:       const providerTasks = { ...(job.providerTasks ?? {}), [cameraId]: { taskId, submittedAt: FieldValue.serverTimestamp() } };\n397:       const cameraAttempts = { ...(job.cameraAttempts ?? {}) } as Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>;\n398:       cameraAttempts[cameraId] = { ...(cameraAttempts[cameraId] ?? {}), submissionState: \"submitted\" };\n399:       transaction.update(ref, { providerTasks, cameraAttempts, timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp() });\n400:     });\n401:   }\n402: \n403:   async recordSubmissionFailure(\n404:     input: RequestGenerationInput,\n405:     cameraId: CameraId,\n406:     errorCode: string,\n407:     certainty: \"non_billable\" | \"unknown\",\n408:   ): Promise<void> {\n409:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, input.partyId, input.jobId);\n410:     const budget = budgetRef(this.db, input.partyId);\n411:     await this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n412:       const [snapshot, budgetSnapshot] = await Promise.all([transaction.get(ref), transaction.get(budget)]);\n413:       if (!snapshot.exists) return;\n414:       const job = snapshot.data()!;\n415:       const cameraAttempts = { ...(job.cameraAttempts ?? {}) } as Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>;\n416:       cameraAttempts[cameraId] = {\n417:         ...(cameraAttempts[cameraId] ?? {}),\n418:         submissionState: certainty === \"non_billable\" ? \"rejected_non_billable\" : \"submitting\",\n419:         submissionErrorCode: errorCode,\n420:       };\n421:       transaction.update(ref, {\n422:         cameraAttempts,\n423:         state: certainty === \"unknown\" ? \"running\" : \"failed\",\n424:         status: certainty === \"unknown\" ? \"reconciliation_required\" : \"failed\",\n425:         errorCode: \"PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE\",\n426:         ...(certainty === \"unknown\" ? { reconciliationReason: \"SUBMISSION_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN\" } : {}),\n427:         ...(certainty === \"non_billable\" ? { failedAt: FieldValue.serverTimestamp() } : {}),\n428:         timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n429:         workerLeaseUntilMs: 0,\n430:       });\n431:       if (certainty === \"non_billable\" && budgetSnapshot.exists && budgetSnapshot.data()?.activeJobId === input.jobId) {\n432:         transaction.update(budget, { activeJobId: null, state: \"idle\", updatedAt: FieldValue.serverTimestamp() });\n433:       }\n434:     });\n435:   }\n436: \n437:   async recordCameraResult(\n438:     partyId: string,\n439:     jobId: string,\n440:     cameraId: CameraId,\n441:     result: ProviderResult,\n442:     taskStatus: ProviderTaskStatus,\n443:     staged: Record<string, unknown>,\n444:   ): Promise<void> {\n445:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, partyId, jobId);\n446:     await this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n447:       const snapshot = await transaction.get(ref);\n448:       if (!snapshot.exists) throw new BackendError(\"NOT_FOUND\", \"Generation job does not exist.\");\n449:       const job = snapshot.data()!;\n450:       const stagedOutputs = { ...(job.stagedOutputs ?? {}), [cameraId]: staged };\n451:       const cameraResults = { ...(job.cameraResults ?? {}), [cameraId]: {\n452:         secondsOut: result.secondsOut,\n453:         secondsIn: result.secondsIn,\n454:         creditsCharged: result.creditsCharged,\n455:         providerState: taskStatus.state,\n456:       } };\n457:       const cameraAttempts = { ...(job.cameraAttempts ?? {}) } as Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>;\n458:       cameraAttempts[cameraId] = { ...(cameraAttempts[cameraId] ?? {}), submissionState: \"complete\", providerState: taskStatus.state };\n459:       transaction.update(ref, {\n460:         stagedOutputs,\n461:         cameraResults,\n462:         cameraAttempts,\n463:         timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n464:       });\n465:     });\n466:   }\n467: \n468:   /** Fixture slot outcome: no provider task, truthful fixture provenance. */\n469:   async recordFixtureResult(\n470:     partyId: string,\n471:     jobId: string,\n472:     cameraId: CameraId,\n473:     staged: Record<string, unknown>,\n474:     secondsOut = 2,\n475:   ): Promise<void> {\n476:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, partyId, jobId);\n477:     await this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n478:       const snapshot = await transaction.get(ref);\n479:       if (!snapshot.exists) throw new BackendError(\"NOT_FOUND\", \"Generation job does not exist.\");\n480:       const job = snapshot.data()!;\n481:       transaction.update(ref, {\n482:         stagedOutputs: { ...(job.stagedOutputs ?? {}), [cameraId]: staged },\n483:         cameraResults: {\n484:           ...(job.cameraResults ?? {}),\n485:           [cameraId]: { secondsOut, secondsIn: 0, creditsCharged: null, providerState: \"FIXTURE\" },\n486:         },\n487:         timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n488:       });\n489:     });\n490:   }\n491: \n492:   /** Consent withdrawal fails the bound job closed and releases the party budget. */\n493:   async failForWithdrawnConsent(partyId: string, jobId: string): Promise<void> {\n494:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, partyId, jobId);\n495:     const budget = budgetRef(this.db, partyId);\n496:     await this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n497:       const [snapshot, budgetSnapshot] = await Promise.all([transaction.get(ref), transaction.get(budget)]);\n498:       if (!snapshot.exists) return;\n499:       transaction.update(ref, {\n500:         state: \"failed\",\n501:         status: \"failed\",\n502:         errorCode: \"FORBIDDEN\",\n503:         reconciliationReason: \"GUEST_CONSENT_WITHDRAWN\",\n504:         failedAt: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n505:         timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n506:         workerLeaseUntilMs: 0,\n507:       });\n508:       if (budgetSnapshot.exists && budgetSnapshot.data()?.activeJobId === jobId) {\n509:         transaction.update(budget, { activeJobId: null, state: \"idle\", updatedAt: FieldValue.serverTimestamp() });\n510:       }\n511:     });\n512:   }\n513: \n514:   async recordProviderFailure(input: RequestGenerationInput, cameraId: CameraId, errorCode: string): Promise<void> {\n515:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, input.partyId, input.jobId);\n516:     const budget = budgetRef(this.db, input.partyId);\n517:     await this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n518:       const [jobSnapshot, budgetSnapshot] = await Promise.all([transaction.get(ref), transaction.get(budget)]);\n519:       if (!jobSnapshot.exists) return;\n520:       transaction.update(ref, {\n521:         state: \"failed\",\n522:         status: \"failed\",\n523:         errorCode: \"PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE\",\n524:         providerErrorCode: errorCode.replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_-]/g, \"_\").slice(0, 80),\n525:         failedAt: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n526:         timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n527:         workerLeaseUntilMs: 0,\n528:         [`cameraAttempts.${cameraId}.providerState`]: \"FAILED\",\n529:       });\n530:       if (budgetSnapshot.exists && budgetSnapshot.data()?.activeJobId === input.jobId) {\n531:         transaction.update(budget, { activeJobId: null, state: \"idle\", updatedAt: FieldValue.serverTimestamp() });\n532:       }\n533:     });\n534:   }\n535: \n536:   async recordStagedOutput(partyId: string, jobId: string, cameraId: CameraId, staged: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<void> {\n537:     const ref = jobRef(this.db, partyId, jobId);\n538:     await this.db.runTransaction(async (transaction) => {\n539:       const snapshot = await transaction.get(ref);\n540:       if (!snapshot.exists) throw new BackendError(\"NOT_FOUND\", \"Generation job does not exist.\");\n541:       const job = snapshot.data()!;\n542:       transaction.update(ref, {\n543:         stagedOutputs: { ...(job.stagedOutputs ?? {}), [cameraId]: staged },\n544:         timestamp: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(),\n545:       });\n546:     });\n547:   }\n548: \n549:   async releaseWorker(partyId: string, jobId: string): Promise<void> {\n550:     await jobRef(this.db, partyId, jobId).update({ workerLeaseUntilMs: 0, timestamp: