{"type":"text","timestamp":1793461315878,"sessionID":"ses_e6d6514fcffe8tXblUpqWJRce4","part":{"id":"prt_1929fe925001b7CoebyXJFY68b","sessionID":"ses_e6d6514fcffe8tXblUpqWJRce4","messageID":"msg_1929fe1eb001YXPzdimfc2JEjH","type":"text","text":"Types compile — now documenting contracts and rationale.","time":{"start":1793461315877,"end":1793461315878}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793461318418,"sessionID":"ses_e6d6514fcffe8tXblUpqWJRce4","part":{"partID":"prt_1929fe927001Z4YJka23z181OI","sessionID":"ses_e6d6514fcffe8tXblUpqWJRce4","messageID":"msg_1929fe1eb001YXPzdimfc2JEjH","type":"tool","id":"call_01a1929fe71c714cb7d3b75d3e92bb1e","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"Firestore layout: `parties/{partyId}` (`ownerUid`, `status`, `activeChannelId`),\n`channels/{channelId}`, `manifests/current_{channelId}` (`version`,\n`cameraClips[1|2|4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n`jobs/{jobId}` (state machine\n`queued → running → ready → delivering → purged`, plus `failed`/`expired` with\nsanitized `errorCode`, `modelId`, `costEstimate`), `devices/{deviceId}`,\n`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`, `hostInvites/{inviteId}` (token hash, party/channel/\nexpiry binding), `seedVideos/{seedId}` (status, job link, preview refs).\n\nStorage layout: `parties/{partyId}/channels/{channelId}/delivery/{version}/{camera}.mp4`\n(served only via short-lived signed URLs minted after callable checks; rules\ndeny all direct client reads/writes). `hostPreviews/{seedId}/{camera}.mp4`\nare separately referenced preview objects with their own TTL metadata (same\ndeny-all rules; signed on demand, never persisted). `ingest/` and\n`generated/{jobId}/`\nprefixes are worker-internal. Lifecycle TTL (`storage.lifecycle.json`,\n`daysSinceCustomTime: 1` on `parties/`) is defense-in-depth behind\n`sweepExpiredMedia`.\n\n## Camera counts (configurable 1/2/4 layouts)\n\nSupported manifest clip counts are exactly 1, 2, or 4; four remains the\ndefault when the `cameraCount` setting is absent, invalid, or unreadable.\n`cameraCount` (a SettingsPort display cap, owned by other partitions) never\nchanges what the backend publishes: generation presets keep producing 4\nclips, and reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete received\nmanifest. Validators on both sides (`validateCctvManifest` in\n`core_playlist`, `validateCanonicalClips`/`parseAck` in `contracts.ts`,\nDart delivery URL/ACK checks in `firebase_delivery_client.dart`) require the\ncamera set to equal the first-N canonical slots in wall order\n(`CAM-01` for 1; `CAM-01`–`CAM-02` for 2; all four for 4). Reordered valid\nclips remain accepted; unsupported counts, gaps (e.g. `{CAM-01, CAM-03}`\nfor count 2), duplicates, unknown cameras, and invalid existing metadata\nare rejected. ACK validation is exact at acceptance: the hash set must equal\nthe actual manifest's camera set with identical digests, so extra hashes are\nrejected both at shape time (`parseAck`) and against the stored manifest\n(`canonicalClipsMatch`) and on accepted-ACK replay. Legacy four-camera\nfixture hashes and the ACK idempotency key are unchanged\n(`test/fixtures/backend_contract_v1.json`); count vectors live in\n`test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json`.\n\n## Host entry and administration\n\nThe companion uses a dedicated host entry screen (`HostEntryScreen` with\nScan Host QR + an explicit Join-as-guest route; companion/TV UI owned by\nother partitions). Rationale: guest PIN admission is intentionally broad —\nanyone who can see the TV screen can self-register as a guest with full\nparty-scoped read/generate/ACK power — so host administration must never be\nreachable through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string. A separate\nserver-minted, short-lived invite capability keeps the two routes visibly\ndistinct and makes the privilege boundary auditable: the QR payload, the\nFirestore role, and the callable gates all distinguish host from guest.\n\n- `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\n  registered device with `role: \"tv\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\n  (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\n  once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored at\n  `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to party/channel/expiry.\n- `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken }` redeems the invite\n  transactionally for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned\n  host role. Same-device redemption retries are idempotent (`created:\n  false`); other-device replay, expiry, cross-party/cross-channel reuse,\n  guest PIN reuse (six-digit strings are shape-rejected as tokens), and\n  client-supplied role fields (ignored; the role is always written\n  server-side) can never grant host access.\n- Legacy `joinParty` remains guest-only: it writes `role: \"guest\"`\n  server-side, rejects re-registration of non-guest (host/tv) device docs,\n  and never upgrades a role.\n- Every administrative operation (`listHostVideos`, `generateHostVideo`,\n  `getHostVideoPreview`, `deleteHostVideo`) revalidates the registered host\n  role and party/channel scope (`assertRegisteredHostDevice`); guests get\n  `FORBIDDEN`. Role examples live in `test/fixtures/join_roles_v1.json`.\n\n## Host seed catalog\n\n`listHostVideos` serves a server-backed seed catalog at\n`parties/{partyId}/seedVideos/{seedId}` containing generation status and\ncamera video references. `generateHostVideo { partyId, deviceId, channelId,\nseedId, idempotencyKey, presetId?, guestMediaId? }` is a scoped entry point\nto the existing fixed-preset queue with the same idempotency, single-flight\nbudget, and consent checks as `requestGeneration` (the backing job is\n`hv-{seedId}`); queue deduplication and rebinding refusal behave identically.\n`getHostVideoPreview { …, seedId }` materializes separately referenced,\nTTL-limited (`HOST_PREVIEW_TTL_MS`, 24h) preview objects under\n`hostPreviews/{seedId}/…` before delivery objects can be ACK-purged and\nsigns them on demand without persisting signed URLs.\n\nDeletion granularity and expiry: `deleteHostVideo { …, seedIds[] }`\n(deleted per selected seed id) removes the seed entries and their associated\npreview + delivery objects, revokes an affected current manifest whose jobId\nmatches a deleted seed, and preserves accounting records (costLogs/usage\nledger rows are never deleted). A job tombstone (`hostDeleted`) is written\ntransactionally so deletion/withdrawal races can neither republish (the\npublish path rechecks the tombstone inside its transaction) nor recreate\npreviews (deleted seeds return `NOT_FOUND` and never copy again). Guest\nwithdrawal of a bound submission deletes retained host previews, fails the\nbound seed closed, and tombstones the job; the retention sweep protects live\nseed previews from the orphan pass and purges expired/deleted ones. Direct\nclient access to invites, seeds, and previews remains denied (callable-only\nFirestore docs and Storage objects; previews are served only through signed\nURLs).","oldString":"Firestore layout: `parties/{partyId}` (`ownerUid`, `status`, `activeChannelId`),\n`channels/{channelId}`, `manifests/current_{channelId}` (`version`,\n`cameraClips[4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n`jobs/{jobId}` (state machine\n`queued → running → ready → delivering → purged`, plus `failed`/`expired` with\nsanitized `errorCode`, `modelId`, `costEstimate`), `devices/{deviceId}`,\n`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`.\n\nStorage layout: `parties/{partyId}/channels/{channelId}/delivery/{version}/{camera}.mp4`\n(served only via short-lived signed URLs minted after callable checks; rules\ndeny all direct client reads/writes). `ingest/` and `generated/{jobId}/`\nprefixes are worker-internal. Lifecycle TTL (`storage.lifecycle.json`,\n`daysSinceCustomTime: 1` on `parties/`) is defense-in-depth behind\n`sweepExpiredMedia`.","path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-1/docs/backend-contract-v1.md"},"output":"Edited docs/backend-contract-v1.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"docs/backend-contract-v1.md","patch":"Index: docs/backend-contract-v1.md\n===================================================================\n--- docs/backend-contract-v1.md\n+++ docs/backend-contract-v1.md\n@@ -44,21 +44,108 @@\n `storage.rules`, signed URLs bypass rules with backend validation).\n \n Firestore layout: `parties/{partyId}` (`ownerUid`, `status`, `activeChannelId`),\n `channels/{channelId}`, `manifests/current_{channelId}` (`version`,\n-`cameraClips[4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n+`cameraClips[1|2|4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n `jobs/{jobId}` (state machine\n `queued → running → ready → delivering → purged`, plus `failed`/`expired` with\n sanitized `errorCode`, `modelId`, `costEstimate`), `devices/{deviceId}`,\n-`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`.\n+`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`, `hostInvites/{inviteId}` (token hash, party/channel/\n+expiry binding), `seedVideos/{seedId}` (status, job link, preview refs).\n \n Storage layout: `parties/{partyId}/channels/{channelId}/delivery/{version}/{camera}.mp4`\n (served only via short-lived signed URLs minted after callable checks; rules\n-deny all direct client reads/writes). `ingest/` and `generated/{jobId}/`\n+deny all direct client reads/writes). `hostPreviews/{seedId}/{camera}.mp4`\n+are separately referenced preview objects with their own TTL metadata (same\n+deny-all rules; signed on demand, never persisted). `ingest/` and\n+`generated/{jobId}/`\n prefixes are worker-internal. Lifecycle TTL (`storage.lifecycle.json`,\n `daysSinceCustomTime: 1` on `parties/`) is defense-in-depth behind\n `sweepExpiredMedia`.\n \n+## Camera counts (configurable 1/2/4 layouts)\n+\n+Supported manifest clip counts are exactly 1, 2, or 4; four remains the\n+default when the `cameraCount` setting is absent, invalid, or unreadable.\n+`cameraCount` (a SettingsPort display cap, owned by other partitions) never\n+changes what the backend publishes: generation presets keep producing 4\n+clips, and reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete received\n+manifest. Validators on both sides (`validateCctvManifest` in\n+`core_playlist`, `validateCanonicalClips`/`parseAck` in `contracts.ts`,\n+Dart delivery URL/ACK checks in `firebase_delivery_client.dart`) require the\n+camera set to equal the first-N canonical slots in wall order\n+(`CAM-01` for 1; `CAM-01`–`CAM-02` for 2; all four for 4). Reordered valid\n+clips remain accepted; unsupported counts, gaps (e.g. `{CAM-01, CAM-03}`\n+for count 2), duplicates, unknown cameras, and invalid existing metadata\n+are rejected. ACK validation is exact at acceptance: the hash set must equal\n+the actual manifest's camera set with identical digests, so extra hashes are\n+rejected both at shape time (`parseAck`) and against the stored manifest\n+(`canonicalClipsMatch`) and on accepted-ACK replay. Legacy four-camera\n+fixture hashes and the ACK idempotency key are unchanged\n+(`test/fixtures/backend_contract_v1.json`); count vectors live in\n+`test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json`.\n+\n+## Host entry and administration\n+\n+The companion uses a dedicated host entry screen (`HostEntryScreen` with\n+Scan Host QR + an explicit Join-as-guest route; companion/TV UI owned by\n+other partitions). Rationale: guest PIN admission is intentionally broad —\n+anyone who can see the TV screen can self-register as a guest with full\n+party-scoped read/generate/ACK power — so host administration must never be\n+reachable through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string. A separate\n+server-minted, short-lived invite capability keeps the two routes visibly\n+distinct and makes the privilege boundary auditable: the QR payload, the\n+Firestore role, and the callable gates all distinguish host from guest.\n+\n+- `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\n+  registered device with `role: \"tv\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\n+  (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\n+  once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored at\n+  `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to party/channel/expiry.\n+- `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken }` redeems the invite\n+  transactionally for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned\n+  host role. Same-device redemption retries are idempotent (`created:\n+  false`); other-device replay, expiry, cross-party/cross-channel reuse,\n+  guest PIN reuse (six-digit strings are shape-rejected as tokens), and\n+  client-supplied role fields (ignored; the role is always written\n+  server-side) can never grant host access.\n+- Legacy `joinParty` remains guest-only: it writes `role: \"guest\"`\n+  server-side, rejects re-registration of non-guest (host/tv) device docs,\n+  and never upgrades a role.\n+- Every administrative operation (`listHostVideos`, `generateHostVideo`,\n+  `getHostVideoPreview`, `deleteHostVideo`) revalidates the registered host\n+  role and party/channel scope (`assertRegisteredHostDevice`); guests get\n+  `FORBIDDEN`. Role examples live in `test/fixtures/join_roles_v1.json`.\n+\n+## Host seed catalog\n+\n+`listHostVideos` serves a server-backed seed catalog at\n+`parties/{partyId}/seedVideos/{seedId}` containing generation status and\n+camera video references. `generateHostVideo { partyId, deviceId, channelId,\n+seedId, idempotencyKey, presetId?, guestMediaId? }` is a scoped entry point\n+to the existing fixed-preset queue with the same idempotency, single-flight\n+budget, and consent checks as `requestGeneration` (the backing job is\n+`hv-{seedId}`); queue deduplication and rebinding refusal behave identically.\n+`getHostVideoPreview { …, seedId }` materializes separately referenced,\n+TTL-limited (`HOST_PREVIEW_TTL_MS`, 24h) preview objects under\n+`hostPreviews/{seedId}/…` before delivery objects can be ACK-purged and\n+signs them on demand without persisting signed URLs.\n+\n+Deletion granularity and expiry: `deleteHostVideo { …, seedIds[] }`\n+(deleted per selected seed id) removes the seed entries and their associated\n+preview + delivery objects, revokes an affected current manifest whose jobId\n+matches a deleted seed, and preserves accounting records (costLogs/usage\n+ledger rows are never deleted). A job tombstone (`hostDeleted`) is written\n+transactionally so deletion/withdrawal races can neither republish (the\n+publish path rechecks the tombstone inside its transaction) nor recreate\n+previews (deleted seeds return `NOT_FOUND` and never copy again). Guest\n+withdrawal of a bound submission deletes retained host previews, fails the\n+bound seed closed, and tombstones the job; the retention sweep protects live\n+seed previews from the orphan pass and purges expired/deleted ones. Direct\n+client access to invites, seeds, and previews remains denied (callable-only\n+Firestore docs and Storage objects; previews are served only through signed\n+URLs).\n+\n ## Payloads\n \n - `requestGeneration { partyId, deviceId, channelId, jobId, idempotencyKey, presetId }`\n   — `presetId` must be `\"cheap_demo\"`; any other model/preset field is rejected\n","status":"modified","additions":90,"deletions":3}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited docs/backend-contract-v1.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a1929fe71c714cb7d3b75d3e92bb1e"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"Firestore layout: `parties/{partyId}` (`ownerUid`, `status`, `activeChannelId`),\\n`channels/{channelId}`, `manifests/current_{channelId}` (`version`,\\n`cameraClips[1|2|4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\\n`jobs/{jobId}` (state machine\\n`queued → running → ready → delivering → purged`, plus `failed`/`expired` with\\nsanitized `errorCode`, `modelId`, `costEstimate`), `devices/{deviceId}`,\\n`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`, `hostInvites/{inviteId}` (token hash, party/channel/\\nexpiry binding), `seedVideos/{seedId}` (status, job link, preview refs).\\n\\nStorage layout: `parties/{partyId}/channels/{channelId}/delivery/{version}/{camera}.mp4`\\n(served only via short-lived signed URLs minted after callable checks; rules\\ndeny all direct client reads/writes). `hostPreviews/{seedId}/{camera}.mp4`\\nare separately referenced preview objects with their own TTL metadata (same\\ndeny-all rules; signed on demand, never persisted). `ingest/` and\\n`generated/{jobId}/`\\nprefixes are worker-internal. Lifecycle TTL (`storage.lifecycle.json`,\\n`daysSinceCustomTime: 1` on `parties/`) is defense-in-depth behind\\n`sweepExpiredMedia`.\\n\\n## Camera counts (configurable 1/2/4 layouts)\\n\\nSupported manifest clip counts are exactly 1, 2, or 4; four remains the\\ndefault when the `cameraCount` setting is absent, invalid, or unreadable.\\n`cameraCount` (a SettingsPort display cap, owned by other partitions) never\\nchanges what the backend publishes: generation presets keep producing 4\\nclips, and reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete received\\nmanifest. Validators on both sides (`validateCctvManifest` in\\n`core_playlist`, `validateCanonicalClips`/`parseAck` in `contracts.ts`,\\nDart delivery URL/ACK checks in `firebase_delivery_client.dart`) require the\\ncamera set to equal the first-N canonical slots in wall order\\n(`CAM-01` for 1; `CAM-01`–`CAM-02` for 2; all four for 4). Reordered valid\\nclips remain accepted; unsupported counts, gaps (e.g. `{CAM-01, CAM-03}`\\nfor count 2), duplicates, unknown cameras, and invalid existing metadata\\nare rejected. ACK validation is exact at acceptance: the hash set must equal\\nthe actual manifest's camera set with identical digests, so extra hashes are\\nrejected both at shape time (`parseAck`) and against the stored manifest\\n(`canonicalClipsMatch`) and on accepted-ACK replay. Legacy four-camera\\nfixture hashes and the ACK idempotency key are unchanged\\n(`test/fixtures/backend_contract_v1.json`); count vectors live in\\n`test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json`.\\n\\n## Host entry and administration\\n\\nThe companion uses a dedicated host entry screen (`HostEntryScreen` with\\nScan Host QR + an explicit Join-as-guest route; companion/TV UI owned by\\nother partitions). Rationale: guest PIN admission is intentionally broad —\\nanyone who can see the TV screen can self-register as a guest with full\\nparty-scoped read/generate/ACK power — so host administration must never be\\nreachable through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string. A separate\\nserver-minted, short-lived invite capability keeps the two routes visibly\\ndistinct and makes the privilege boundary auditable: the QR payload, the\\nFirestore role, and the callable gates all distinguish host from guest.\\n\\n- `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\\n  registered device with `role: \\\"tv\\\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\\n  (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\\n  once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored at\\n  `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to party/channel/expiry.\\n- `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken }` redeems the invite\\n  transactionally for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned\\n  host role. Same-device redemption retries are idempotent (`created:\\n  false`); other-device replay, expiry, cross-party/cross-channel reuse,\\n  guest PIN reuse (six-digit strings are shape-rejected as tokens), and\\n  client-supplied role fields (ignored; the role is always written\\n  server-side) can never grant host access.\\n- Legacy `joinParty` remains guest-only: it writes `role: \\\"guest\\\"`\\n  server-side, rejects re-registration of non-guest (host/tv) device docs,\\n  and never upgrades a role.\\n- Every administrative operation (`listHostVideos`, `generateHostVideo`,\\n  `getHostVideoPreview`, `deleteHostVideo`) revalidates the registered host\\n  role and party/channel scope (`assertRegisteredHostDevice`); guests get\\n  `FORBIDDEN`. Role examples live in `test/fixtures/join_roles_v1.json`.\\n\\n## Host seed catalog\\n\\n`listHostVideos` serves a server-backed seed catalog at\\n`parties/{partyId}/seedVideos/{seedId}` containing generation status and\\ncamera video references. `generateHostVideo { partyId, deviceId, channelId,\\nseedId, idempotencyKey, presetId?, guestMediaId? }` is a scoped entry point\\nto the existing fixed-preset queue with the same idempotency, single-flight\\nbudget, and consent checks as `requestGeneration` (the backing job is\\n`hv-{seedId}`); queue deduplication and rebinding refusal behave identically.\\n`getHostVideoPreview { …, seedId }` materializes separately referenced,\\nTTL-limited (`HOST_PREVIEW_TTL_MS`, 24h) preview objects under\\n`hostPreviews/{seedId}/…` before delivery objects can be ACK-purged and\\nsigns them on demand without persisting signed URLs.\\n\\nDeletion granularity and expiry: `deleteHostVideo { …, seedIds[] }`\\n(deleted per selected seed id) removes the seed entries and their associated\\npreview + delivery objects, revokes an affected current manifest whose jobId\\nmatches a deleted seed, and preserves accounting records (costLogs/usage\\nledger rows are never deleted). A job tombstone (`hostDeleted`) is written\\ntransactionally so deletion/withdrawal races can neither republish (the\\npublish path rechecks the tombstone inside its transaction) nor recreate\\npreviews (deleted seeds return `NOT_FOUND` and never copy again). Guest\\nwithdrawal of a bound submission deletes retained host previews, fails the\\nbound seed closed, and tombstones the job; the retention sweep protects live\\nseed previews from the orphan pass and purges expired/deleted ones. Direct\\nclient access to invites, seeds, and previews remains denied (callable-only\\nFirestore docs and Storage objects; previews are served only through signed\\nURLs).\",\"oldString\":\"Firestore layout: `parties/{partyId}` (`ownerUid`, `status`, `activeChannelId`),\\n`channels/{channelId}`, `manifests/current_{channelId}` (`version`,\\n`cameraClips[4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\\n`jobs/{jobId}` (state machine\\n`queued → running → ready → delivering → purged`, plus `failed`/`expired` with\\nsanitized `errorCode`, `modelId`, `costEstimate`), `devices/{deviceId}`,\\n`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`.\\n\\nStorage layout: `parties/{partyId}/channels/{channelId}/delivery/{version}/{camera}.mp4`\\n(served only via short-lived signed URLs minted after callable checks; rules\\ndeny all direct client reads/writes). `ingest/` and `generated/{jobId}/`\\nprefixes are worker-internal. Lifecycle TTL (`storage.lifecycle.json`,\\n`daysSinceCustomTime: 1` on `parties/`) is defense-in-depth behind\\n`sweepExpiredMedia`.\",\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-1/docs/backend-contract-v1.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793461315879,"end":1793461318418}}}}
