{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793461325781,"sessionID":"ses_e6d6514fcffe8tXblUpqWJRce4","part":{"id":"prt_192a00fd5001mwCifuQa43MLoc","sessionID":"ses_e6d6514fcffe8tXblUpqWJRce4","messageID":"msg_192a009a5001ebuGTIHFo0nWrP","type":"step-start","snapshot":"178e078401d603accbf747c9926edecdcac00d33"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793461326235,"sessionID":"ses_e6d6514fcffe8tXblUpqWJRce4","part":{"partID":"prt_192a00fde001k5RYP2SyoX6wZF","sessionID":"ses_e6d6514fcffe8tXblUpqWJRce4","messageID":"msg_192a009a5001ebuGTIHFo0nWrP","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192a00cd37496be8f8c1c4cc84811","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# core_playlist\n\nPlayback manifest domain model for Halloween TV: CCTV camera contracts,\nmanifest parsing, and validation shared by every layer.\n\n## Camera identity (single source of truth)\n\n`cctvSlots` is the canonical wall order, camera ids (`CAM-01`–`CAM-04`),\nand default room labels. Tile maps, asset catalogs, and label resolution\nderive from it; no `CAM-0x` literals are duplicated in other layers.\n\n## Configurable 1/2/4-camera layouts\n\nSupported manifest clip counts are exactly **1, 2, or 4**\n(`kSupportedCctvClipCounts`); **four is the default** when the\n`cameraCount` setting (a SettingsPort display cap owned outside this\npackage) is absent, invalid, or unreadable (`kDefaultCctvClipCount`).\n\n- `isSupportedCctvClipCount` / `expectedCctvCameraIds` are the shared\n  prefix helpers: a count-`N` manifest must carry exactly the first `N`\n  canonical slot ids in wall order. Backend `contracts.ts`\n  (`SUPPORTED_CAMERA_COUNTS`, `expectedCameraIds`) mirrors them.\n- `validateCctvManifest` accepts 1, 2, or 4 clips with unique clip ids and\n  a camera set equal to the first-`N` prefix. Reordered valid clips remain\n  accepted; unsupported counts, gaps (e.g. `{CAM-01, CAM-03}` for count 2),\n  duplicates, unknown cameras, and invalid existing metadata are rejected.\n- The cap is display-only: generation presets keep producing 4 clips, and\n  reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete received manifest\n  (see `PreparePlayback` and the delivery ACK client).\n- Count vectors live in `test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json`; the legacy\n  four-camera hashes are preserved byte-identically.\n\n## Host entry rationale (pointer)\n\nThe companion uses a dedicated host entry screen (`HostEntryScreen` with\nScan Host QR + an explicit Join-as-guest route) so host administration can\nnever be reached through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string.\nThe contract half of that boundary (server-minted invites, server-assigned\nhost role, host-gated seed catalog) is documented in\n`docs/backend-contract-v1.md`; this package only carries the camera-count\nside of the shared contracts.\n","path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-1/packages/core_playlist/README.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully: packages/core_playlist/README.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wrote file successfully: packages/core_playlist/README.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192a00cd37496be8f8c1c4cc84811"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# core_playlist\\n\\nPlayback manifest domain model for Halloween TV: CCTV camera contracts,\\nmanifest parsing, and validation shared by every layer.\\n\\n## Camera identity (single source of truth)\\n\\n`cctvSlots` is the canonical wall order, camera ids (`CAM-01`–`CAM-04`),\\nand default room labels. Tile maps, asset catalogs, and label resolution\\nderive from it; no `CAM-0x` literals are duplicated in other layers.\\n\\n## Configurable 1/2/4-camera layouts\\n\\nSupported manifest clip counts are exactly **1, 2, or 4**\\n(`kSupportedCctvClipCounts`); **four is the default** when the\\n`cameraCount` setting (a SettingsPort display cap owned outside this\\npackage) is absent, invalid, or unreadable (`kDefaultCctvClipCount`).\\n\\n- `isSupportedCctvClipCount` / `expectedCctvCameraIds` are the shared\\n  prefix helpers: a count-`N` manifest must carry exactly the first `N`\\n  canonical slot ids in wall order. Backend `contracts.ts`\\n  (`SUPPORTED_CAMERA_COUNTS`, `expectedCameraIds`) mirrors them.\\n- `validateCctvManifest` accepts 1, 2, or 4 clips with unique clip ids and\\n  a camera set equal to the first-`N` prefix. Reordered valid clips remain\\n  accepted; unsupported counts, gaps (e.g. `{CAM-01, CAM-03}` for count 2),\\n  duplicates, unknown cameras, and invalid existing metadata are rejected.\\n- The cap is display-only: generation presets keep producing 4 clips, and\\n  reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete received manifest\\n  (see `PreparePlayback` and the delivery ACK client).\\n- Count vectors live in `test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json`; the legacy\\n  four-camera hashes are preserved byte-identically.\\n\\n## Host entry rationale (pointer)\\n\\nThe companion uses a dedicated host entry screen (`HostEntryScreen` with\\nScan Host QR + an explicit Join-as-guest route) so host administration can\\nnever be reached through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string.\\nThe contract half of that boundary (server-minted invites, server-assigned\\nhost role, host-gated seed catalog) is documented in\\n`docs/backend-contract-v1.md`; this package only carries the camera-count\\nside of the shared contracts.\\n\",\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-1/packages/core_playlist/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793461325791,"end":1793461326235}}}}
